  TODO before this is usable in a real device tree build:
  - The stock <sepolicy><version>27.0</version></sepolicy> and the
    compatibility_matrix.xml <vndk><version>0.0.0</version></vndk> reflect
    Samsung's non-Treble HIDL-wrapper scheme, not a real VNDK-versioned
    vendor. Both need to be re-set to match whatever Android version this
    device tree actually targets once that's decided.
  - HAL interface versions below (e.g. keymaster@3.0, graphics.composer@2.1)
    are what stock Oreo shipped. A from-source rebuild may reimplement some
    of these against newer HAL versions depending on target Android version -
    verify each one against what universal7870-common/kernel actually expose.
  - target-level attribute is absent (old manifest schema) - add one once
    a target Android version is picked.
-->
